# Visual Studio and .NET Core files
## Ignore Visual Studio temporary files, build results, and user-specific settings
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.log
*.pdb
*.opendb
*.dbmdl

## Build results
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
[Oo]ut/
build/
dist/
publish/

## NuGet packages
packages/
.nuget/
project.lock.json # Old .NET Core lock file
# project.assets.json is usually inside obj/ and covered by obj/

## Rider IDE files
.idea/
*.sln.DotSettings
*.csproj.DotSettings

## VS Code IDE files
.vscode/

## Resharper files
*.resharper
*.DotSettings.user

## Test results
TestResults/
*.trx

## SQL Server files (local development databases)
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.sdf
*.bak
*.dacpac

## Environment-specific configuration files (sensitive data or local overrides)
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Production.json
appsettings.Staging.json
appsettings.Test.json
# Keep appsettings.json for default values

## Client-side dependencies (if any, common for web projects)
node_modules/
bower_components/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
yarn-debug.log

## Other common temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*.userprefs
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db